&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Iran has &quot;substantially increased&quot; efforts to target American diplomats and officials in the Middle East and other nations, according to a US intelligence memo addressed to US Secretary of State Marco Rubio cited by Axios. The intel also warned that plots targeting US diplomats were reaching &quot;advanced stages&quot;..&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the one-page memo sent to Rubio on October 23, US officials expressed concern that Iran-backed Houthi rebels in Yemen could widen the scope of their attacks beyond Saudi Arabia to other countries in the region, Axios reported.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Director of National Intelligence Jay Clayton also warned Rubio that intelligence about the alleged assassination plots by Iran must reach more US personnel than are currently authorised to receive it.&lt;/p&gt;
